{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>He killed</b> — by way of simile, like <i>you shall stone them</i>." "<b>And their sycamores</b> — feminine form, though sycamores are masculine, like נפשות נפשותם. Hasā'ōn said: כי בחנמל is a species of locust, and he explained חנמל as two words. But in my opinion: כי בחנמל — hail, like great stones from the sky, for it corresponds to <i>hail</i>, and sycamores have fruit like figs, and the word חנמל is a compound."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The lemma יהרג ('He killed') from the verse is rendered; the comparison is to the idiom of stoning as figurative.", 1 "Resolved epithet הסאון / חסאון as 'Hasā'ōn' (reference uncertain; possibly a known grammarian or a corrupted name). The final phrase 'מלת חנמל רבעית' appears corrupt or abbreviated; rendered hyper-literally as 'a compound' based on the context of the preceding interpretation, but the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:17.038130702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}